    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Ethiopia_Regional_State (established 19 August 2023; Wolayita, Gamo, Gofa, Gedeo, South Omo, Ari, Konso, Gardula, Burji, Koore, Basketo, and Ale zones; 45,209 km²)"
  ],
  "notes": "Built from the 74 zones of geoBoundaries ADM2 (2016 names) merged into regions, not carved from ADM1, because the clipper fails on the Sidama zone's edge; the merged regions match ADM1's areas to within 10 km². Zones standing in for later ones: Bench Maji for Bench Sheko and West Omo; KT for Kembata and the Tembaro special woreda; Gurage for Gurage, East Gurage, and the Kebena and Mareko special woredas; Gamo Gofa for Gamo and Gofa; South Omo for South Omo and Ari; Segen Peoples' for Konso, Burji, Koore (Amaro), Gardula (Derashe), and Ale. Every later unit is a whole part of one 2016 zone, so nothing is approximate in composition. Sidama zone (6,909 km²) includes Hawassa. Areas built: South West 38,850 km² (published 39,400), Central 15,271 (15,099), South 48,381 (45,209; includes the Gedeo exclave). The source leaves Lake Tana as a hole in Amhara. Dates: Sidama 18 June 2020 (handover of power), South West 23 November 2021, and Central and South Ethiopia 19 August 2023; the last two rest on Wikipedia and were not checked against a proclamation.",
